+## 8. Lifecycle review follow-up (14 September 2026)
+
+`git-ssh unlock` now proves the managed key can sign after starting the loader;
+a skipped session condition is not success. `git-ssh lock` still works when
+key files are missing or corrupted. The agent remains gated by the active
+Labwc target/compositor. Private credential directories must be mode 0700.
+
+GitOps TERM/HUP cancellation cleans independent Git/SSH child process groups.
+Use canonical policy paths without `./`, `//` or dot components. A rooted
+directory glob such as `vendor/*.keep/` protects every matching subtree and
+locally absent matching paths. Cancellation is not a guarantee against abrupt
+SIGKILL/power loss; inspect status and the printed recovery reference.
+
+`debugsys report --categories security credentials` now includes managed-unit
+PID/user namespace, cgroup and agent lifetime metadata in its overview, without
+reading service environments or decrypting a key. The root-filesystem probe
+shares the overall collection budget. Hook enable/remove behavior is unchanged.
+
+Only the system Bluetooth controller initializer, NVIDIA character-link helper
+and the two zram maintenance/PSI services receive `PrivatePIDs=yes`; they retain
+`PrivateUsers=no`. Power handoff, forking lock, host diagnostics, tmpfs pre-clean,
+SSH agent and key loader are explicitly excluded. This requires systemd 257+ and
+kernel/manager namespace support, and still needs live target acceptance.
+See the repository's `docs/LIFECYCLE-ISOLATION-REVIEW-20260914.md` and
+`docs/validation-lifecycle-20260914/` for selection reasons and actual test results.
